The main theorem `erdos_364` (no consecutive triple of powerful numbers) is a genuinely open research problem in number theory, listed as open on erdosproblems.com/364 and marked `@[category research open]` in the formalization. The strong variant is likewise open. The weak variant (no quadruple) is textbook and already proved in the problem text.

I cannot prove an open conjecture. The no-three-consecutive-powerful-numbers conjecture of Erdős remains unresolved as of my knowledge; powerful-number triples would require n, n+1, n+2 all having the property that every prime divisor p satisfies p² | n, and no argument is known to rule this out (nor is any example known). The standard techniques—modular obstructions (which settle the quadruple case via the 2 mod 4 argument), Pell equation analysis of consecutive powerful pairs, or abc-type estimates—do not currently close the gap for triples.

